        "original_id": "77aa28ad-697e-51dd-a7b2-e6bf30d07212",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Albert Simons, Louis Gourd, Mrs. Louis Gourd\n- Organizations: College of Charleston\n- Places: South Carolina, United States\n- Buildings: School of the Arts building, Louis Gourd House\n- Honors: Simons Medal of Excellence\n\nFacts:\n- The College of Charleston was founded in 1770 and chartered in 1785.\n- The College of Charleston is the oldest college in South Carolina, the 13th oldest institution of higher learning in the United States, and the oldest municipal college in the country.\n- In 1939, Mr. and Mrs. Louis Gourd acquired the Louis Gourd House and quickly hired Charleston architect Albert Simons to plan the remodeling of the building.\n- Albert Simons was a professor at the College of Charleston for over 20 years.\n- Albert Simons started the School of the Arts at the College of Charleston.\n- The School of the Arts building is named after Albert Simons.\n- Albert Simons is honored yearly through the Simons Medal of Excellence.",
